.SH "NAME"
lpm \- Lotus Package Manager
.SS "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fIlpm\fP <command> [options] [package(s)]
.SS "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
\fIlpm\fP is the package manager for Lotus Linux. It installs, removes, upgrades,
and queries binary (\f(CR.lpkg\fP) and source packages built from LPDF v1
\fBPKGBUILD\fP(5) files, resolving dependencies through a DAG resolver and applying
filesystem changes through a journaled transaction layer that rolls back on
failure.
.sp
\fIlpm\fP understands exactly one configuration file, \f(CR/etc/lpm/lpm.conf\fP
(see \fBlpm.conf\fP(5)), and one package\-definition format, LPDF v1 (see
\fBPKGBUILD\fP(5)).
.sp
Run \fIlpm\fP <command> \fI\-\-help\fP for a short summary of any command.
.SS "COMMANDS"
.sp
\fIlpm\fP dispatches on the first argument, which must be one of the commands
below. Only one command may be given at a time.
.SS "Transaction commands"
.sp
These share one output shape: resolve, show a package table, confirm, execute
with a step counter, then print \fITransaction complete.\fP They require root
(via \fIdoas\fP or \fIsudo\fP).
.sp
\fIinstall\fP <package(s)>
.RS 4
Resolve dependencies for the named packages, show the transaction
summary, and after confirmation fetch, build (source packages) or
download\-and\-verify (binary packages) and install each one.
Already\-installed explicit targets are reinstalled.
.RE
.sp
\fIremove\fP <package(s)>
.RS 4
Remove installed packages. With \fI\-Rs\fP/\fI\-\-recursive\fP, also remove
dependencies installed as dependencies that no longer satisfy any
dependency. Blocked, unless \fI\-\-force\fP, when other installed packages
depend on a target.
.RE
.sp
\fIupgrade\fP [package(s)]
.RS 4
With no arguments, synchronise the package databases and upgrade every
installed package with a newer version available. With arguments, check
and upgrade only the named packages. Honours \fIIgnorePkg\fP from
\fBlpm.conf\fP(5).
.RE
.sp
\fIbootstrap\fP \fI\-C\fP <target> [package(s)]
.RS 4
Install a base system into <target>: create the FHS skeleton, write
stub configuration, synchronise databases, then install the named
packages (or the built\-in base set). Also invoked as \fIpacstrap\fP.
.RE
.SS "Non\-transaction commands"
.sp
\fIupdate\fP
.RS 4
Synchronise the package databases from the configured repositories. Not
a transaction: no summary table, no confirmation prompt.
.RE
.sp
\fIsearch\fP <term>
.RS 4
Search available packages (name and description) in the synced
databases, falling back to the local PKGBUILD cache.
.RE
.sp
\fIinfo\fP <package(s)>
.RS 4
Show detailed information about package(s): name, version, repository,
architecture, type, license, dependencies, and sizes.
.RE
.sp
\fIdeps\fP [package(s)]
.RS 4
Print the full dependency tree for the named package(s).
.RE
.sp
\fIlist\fP
.RS 4
List installed packages. Accepts \fI\-\-count\fP to print only the count.
.RE
.sp
\fIowns\fP <path>
.RS 4
Report which installed package owns the given file path.
.RE
.sp
\fIfiles\fP <package>
.RS 4
List the files owned by an installed package.
.RE
.sp
\fIorphans\fP
.RS 4
List packages installed as dependencies that no longer satisfy any
dependency (candidates for \fIremove \-Rs\fP).
.RE
.sp
\fIverify\fP [package(s)]
.RS 4
Verify installed package integrity against recorded metadata: existence,
checksums, permissions, ownership. Read\-only \(em \fIverify\fP never repairs
or rewrites files. With \fI\-\-deps\fP, check dependency consistency instead.
.RE
.sp
\fItest\fP <package(s)>
.RS 4
Run a package\(cqs \fIcheck()\fP test suite from its PKGBUILD.
.RE
.sp
\fIaudit\fP
.RS 4
Show the transaction history (the audit log). With \fI\-\-raw\fP (back\-compat
alias \fI\-\-log\fP) dump the unformatted log; with \fI\-\-health\fP show a quick
orphan/update summary.
.RE
.sp
\fIcache\fP [clean] [package(s)]
.RS 4
With no subcommand, show build\-cache statistics. With \fIclean\fP, remove
cached build data (optionally limited to named packages) after
confirmation.
.RE
.sp
\fIkey\fP <subcommand> [args]
.RS 4
Manage the signing keyring. Subcommands: \fIinit\fP, \fIgenid\fP, \fIlist\fP,
\fIrecv\fP <keyid>, \fIimport\fP <file>, \fItrust\fP <keyid>.
.RE
.sp
\fIpackage\fP <subcommand> [args]
.RS 4
Low\-level package tools. Subcommands: \fIbuild\fP <pkg>, \fIpack\fP <pkg>,
\fIinstall\fP <pkg.lpkg|name>, \fIquery\fP [pkg.lpkg|name], \fIextract\fP
<pkg.lpkg|name>, \fIverify\fP <pkg.lpkg|name>, \fIremove\fP <pkg.lpkg|name>.
.RE
.sp
\fIrepo\fP <subcommand>
.RS 4
Repository management. Currently a placeholder (\fIlist\fP, \fIadd\fP, \fIremove\fP,
\fIsync\fP are reserved, not yet implemented).
.RE
.sp
\fI\-V\fP, \fI\-\-version\fP
.RS 4
Show \fIlpm\fP and \fIlibllpm\fP versions and exit.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-h\fP, \fI\-\-help\fP
.RS 4
Show usage. \fIlpm\fP <command> \fI\-\-help\fP shows command\-specific usage.
.RE
.SS "OPTIONS"
.sp
These are recognised by the transaction commands and parsed from anywhere in
their argument list.
.sp
\fI\-\-force\fP
.RS 4
Override file\- and package\-conflict checks and allow removing
\fICriticalPkg\fP packages.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-\-no\-confirm\fP
.RS 4
Run non\-interactively: never prompt before executing a transaction.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-\-dry\-run\fP, \fI\-n\fP
.RS 4
Simulate the transaction and print exactly what would change, with no
side effects.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-\-no\-check\fP
.RS 4
Skip the \fIcheck()\fP phase when building source packages.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-\-no\-recommended\fP
.RS 4
Do not offer \fIrecommends\fP soft\-dependencies during \fIinstall\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-\-strict\fP
.RS 4
Treat a failing \fIcheck()\fP phase as fatal during a source build.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-Rs\fP, \fI\-\-recursive\fP
.RS 4
With \fIremove\fP: also remove now\-unused dependencies.
.RE
.sp
\fI\-\-debug\fP[=\fIN\fP]
.RS 4
Enable debug output to stderr. \fIN\fP is \fI1\fP (dep resolution, cache,
mirrors), \fI2\fP (URLs, checksums), or \fI3\fP (function trace). \fI\-\-debug\fP with
no value is level 1. \fILPM_DEBUG\fP sets the same baseline; \fI\-\-debug=N\fP
overrides it.
.RE
.SS "FILES"
.sp
\fI/etc/lpm/lpm.conf\fP
.RS 4
Main configuration file. See \fBlpm.conf\fP(5).
.RE
.sp
\fI/var/lib/lpm/db\fP
.RS 4
Synchronised package databases (one file per repository).
.RE
.sp
\fI/var/lib/lpm/files\fP
.RS 4
Per\-package file\-ownership records (\fIfiles.list\fP, \fIfiles.meta\fP) used by
\fIverify\fP, \fIowns\fP, and \fIfiles\fP.
.RE
.sp
\fI/var/cache/lpm\fP
.RS 4
Build workspaces, downloaded sources, and built package caches
(\fIBUILDDIR\fP / \fIPKGDEST\fP / \fISRCDEST\fP).
.RE
.sp
\fI/var/log/lpm\fP
.RS 4
Per\-package build logs.
.RE
.SS "EXIT CODES"
.sp
\fI0\fP
.RS 4
Success.
.RE
.sp
\fI1\fP
.RS 4
Generic failure \(em bad usage, unmet dependency, conflict, permission
denied, sync or transaction aborted.
.RE
.sp
\fI130\fP
.RS 4
The operation was interrupted (SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP). The transaction
journal is rolled back and the lock released.
.RE
.SS "NOTES"
.sp
\fIlpm\fP takes an exclusive lock for write operations; only one instance may run
at a time. Interrupting a running transaction prints \fIInterrupted.\fP and
unwinds any partial changes.
.sp
Error conditions use a fixed vocabulary \(em for example \fIPackage not found:
foo\fP, \fIPackage is not installed: foo\fP, \fINo packages to upgrade.\fP, \fINo
orphaned packages.\fP, \fIRepository sync failed.\fP, \fISignature verification
failed.\fP, \fITransaction aborted.\fP, \fIInsufficient disk space.\fP, \fIInterrupted.\fP
.SS "SEE ALSO"
.sp
\fBlpm.conf\fP(5), \fBPKGBUILD\fP(5)
